rows=[
 {'id':'RPF-F070','severity':'high','title':'Challenge score emits VERIFIED without verifying commitment, freeze or cases binding','evidence':ev('invoke/workflow.rs',(593,671))+ev('invoke/tests.rs',(625,685)),'status':'source-established','detail':'run_challenge_score merely deserializes, runs two instances of the same ExactMatchChecker over caller-provided cases, and copies independent commitment/freeze hashes into the result. It never checks challenge IDs, judge commitment, frozen deliverable or linkage between candidate outputs and deliverable. Empty hidden_cases yields VERIFIED by0==0. The happy-path test itself commits text naming two cases but supplies one. Require validated reveal/freeze/manifest linkage and declared nonempty evaluation census before emitting a challenge verification status; distinguish checker duplication from independence.','limits':'Pure source/control-flow finding; this endpoint was not executed in a live challenge. Extends the core challenge binding limitations in RPF-F047/F048 without claiming a private benchmark breach.'},
 {'id':'RPF-F071','severity':'medium','title':'Kitaev adapter names boundary isolation topological protection','evidence':ev('invoke/majorana_math.rs',(200,242)),'status':'source-established claim mismatch','detail':'mzm_topologically_protected is exactly left_isolated && right_isolated, with no spectral-gap, nontrivial-phase or perturbation-stability predicate. A zero Hamiltonian has zero boundary commutators without establishing protected edge physics. Rename this result to the computed boundary-isolation predicate or add and explicitly scope the missing mathematical conditions.','limits':'Adapter source review only; no physical experiment and no claim of a general phase-classification algorithm in the delegated owner.'},
 {'id':'RPF-F072','severity':'high','title':'Surgery verifier certifies a single repeated defect and trusts fabricated counts','evidence':ev('epics/dda.rs',(363,395),(416,431)),'status':'bounded native probe reproduced in both overflow modes','detail':'On d0=[0],d1=[1], fused=(0,0), sigma_before=[1], positive/negative witnesses=[1], sigma_after=[0] receives Verified. This removes one defect, contradicting the advertised exactly-two result. Public counts99/97 also survive verifier and receipt unchanged. Require distinct in-range indices, recompute counts and bind verdict inside receipt construction; add independent forged-pair/count tests.','limits':'Solver-produced pairs are distinct; this failure is in the independent public witness-verification/receipt boundary. No downstream authority promotion or provider run.'},
 {'id':'RPF-F073','severity':'medium','title':'Transport serde bypasses monotone in-range morphism admission','evidence':ev('epics/transport.rs',(121,163),(212,240),(371,390)),'status':'bounded native probe reproduced in both overflow modes','detail':'Derived Deserialize constructs private SimplicialMorphism fields directly. Map[1,0] into2, which new refuses, receives a transport certificate; map[9] into1 reaches unchecked pushforward indexing and panics. Deserialize through validated constructor and validate any public receipt before use.','limits':'Runtime simplicial_transport constructs with new and avoids this particular serde bypass. Public Rust/serde interface still admits it; no external host exploit asserted.'},
 {'id':'RPF-F074','severity':'high','title':'Derivation DAG completeness receipts substitute literal arithmetic for named claim verification','evidence':ev('derivation_dag_witnesses.rs',(237,249),(371,407),(437,469),(959,975),(1724,1779),(2649,2710),(2714,2755)),'status':'source-established; fixed master output reproduced natively','detail':'All33 families pass and list177 unique nodes, but no DAG/paper/dependency/proof inputs are read. Examples: growth minima assigned1; Cabello146 computed2+72+72; Majorana validity assigned comm_trace_zero; completeness counts hard-coded;142 node witnesses depend on index/stage arithmetic rather than named propositions. Tranche7 even compares literals1 and3/4 although its documented R_t(p) formula gives R_1(1)=1. Preserve as illustrative finite fixtures and remove semantic-closure/certification implications, or bind each covered node to an actual owner predicate, premises and checked evidence.','limits':'Some small exact examples and finite CHSH/parity enumerations are valid. This finding does not refute separate paper or Lean proofs; it rejects promoting this native receipt to their verification or to quantum-selection/physical evidence.'},
 {'id':'RPF-F075','severity':'low','title':'Transport chain ledger omits composition carrier compatibility','evidence':ev('epics/transport.rs',(191,205),(309,322)),'status':'bounded native probe reproduced in both overflow modes','detail':'F:[0]->carrier3 and G:[0,1]->carrier2 cannot compose under the public typed dimension rule, yet for_chain(F,G,[0]) returns two loss ledgers because reached indices fit. Check first.target_vertices==then.source_vertices or explicitly expose a restriction/extension morphism and rename the weaker operation.','limits':'The support-relative telescoping count still has its stated elementary interpretation; this is inconsistency with the module composition contract, not a false numerical sum.'}
]
